---
import Tunnel from '../../../layouts/Tunnel.astro';

// THE RUN LIST. NOT A DECISION TREE.
//
// Antonio's insight, and he is right: a DJ two minutes from a set cannot read
// a screen and choose between A and B six times. Under adrenaline the CHOOSING
// is the expensive part, not the doing.
//
// Aviation and emergency medicine solved this long ago: memory items. A short,
// fixed, linear sequence run in order, no branching. The operator stops when
// the problem goes away, and they know it went away because they can hear it.
//
// So the under-60-minutes path is a single screen of actions ordered by
// (how often it works) x (how fast it is). No questions. The DJ works down and
// stops when sound comes out. The decision TREE still exists and is still
// good, it just belongs to the DJ who has an hour or a day, where diagnosis is
// worth more than speed. Link to it at the bottom, not at the top.
---
<Tunnel title="Do This Now | Save My Gig!" status="Critical · Do this now" red srHeading="Do these in order until sound comes out">
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:0.5rem">Do these in order.</h2>
  <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">Stop as soon as it plays. Most DJs are back on by step three.</p>

  <ol class="runlist">
    <li>
      <strong>Pull the USB out. Count to ten. Push it back in firmly.</strong>
      <span>Wait, some drives take 30 seconds to mount.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Try the other slot, then the other player.</strong>
      <span>A drive can fail on one deck and work on the next. If it reads there, play from there.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Playlists missing but the drive shows up? Press FOLDER view.</strong>
      <span>SOURCE, select USB, then the browse / FOLDER button. Your music is still on the stick. You lose cues and sync, you keep the gig.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Load your second USB.</strong>
      <span>If you carry two, this is over in ten seconds.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Wipe the USB tip and try again.</strong>
      <span>Sweat and booth dirt are real causes.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Restart the player, but only if nobody is playing on it.</strong>
      <span>USB STOP first, power off, twenty seconds, back on.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Borrow a drive, or play off your phone into a spare channel.</strong>
      <span>Ask the DJ before or after you. This happens to everyone.</span>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="alert-card" style="margin:1.75rem 0 1.5rem">
    <div style="font-size:20px" aria-hidden="true">⚠️</div>
    <div>
      Do not let anything format or initialise your drive tonight. Your music is
      still on it.
    </div>
  </div>

  <nav class="pad-grid" aria-label="What next">
    <a href="/saved?path=critical&branch=runlist" class="pad pad-green" data-event="outcome_reached" data-outcome="saved" data-path="critical">
      <div class="pad-header">
        <div class="led led-g"></div>
        <div class="pad-title">I AM PLAYING</div>
      </div>
    </a>
    <a href="/protocol/critical" class="pad pad-neutral" data-event="step_completed" data-step="runlist_to_tree">
      <div class="pad-header">
        <div class="led led-n"></div>
        <div class="pad-title">NOTHING WORKED, AND I HAVE TIME</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pad-desc">Step by step diagnosis, one question at a time.</div>
    </a>
  </nav>
</Tunnel>

<style>
  .runlist { list-style: none; counter-reset: rl; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .runlist li {
    counter-increment: rl;
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.85rem 0 0.85rem 2.6rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--edge-soft);
  }
  .runlist li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .runlist li::before {
    content: counter(rl);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.8rem;
    width: 1.85rem;
    height: 1.85rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: var(--surf-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--edge);
    border-radius: 50%;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .runlist strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }
  .runlist span {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.87rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
  @media (max-width: 420px) {
    .runlist li { padding-left: 2.3rem; }
    .runlist strong { font-size: 0.97rem; }
    .runlist span { font-size: 0.83rem; }
  }
</style>
